  "review": {
    "entityID": "person:manasseh_1928",
    "book": "NUM",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "NUM 1:10 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Of the children of Joseph: of Ephraim: Elishama the son of Ammihud; of Manasseh: Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 1:34 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Of the children of Manasseh, their generations, by their families, by their fathers’ houses, according to the number of the names, from twenty years old and upward, all who were able to go out to war:"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 1:35 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "those who were counted of them, of the tribe of Manasseh, were thirty-two thousand two hundred."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 2:20 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Next to him shall be the tribe of Manasseh. The prince of the children of Manasseh shall be Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 7:54 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "On the eighth day Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur, prince of the children of Manasseh,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 10:23 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Gamaliel the son of Pedahzur was over the army of the tribe of the children of Manasseh."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 13:11 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Of the tribe of Joseph, of the tribe of Manasseh, Gaddi the son of Susi."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:28 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The sons of Joseph after their families: Manasseh and Ephraim."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:29 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The sons of Manasseh: of Machir, the family of the Machirites; and Machir became the father of Gilead; of Gilead, the family of the Gileadites."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 26:34 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "These are the families of Manasseh. Those who were counted of them were fifty-two thousand seven hundred."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 27:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Then the daughters of Zelophehad, the son of Hepher, the son of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of Manasseh the son of Joseph came near. These are the names of his daughters: Mahlah, Noah, Hoglah, Milcah, and Tirzah."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 32:33 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses gave to them, even to the children of Gad, and to the children of Reuben, and to the half-tribe of Manasseh the son of Joseph, the kingdom of Sihon king of the Amorites, and the kingdom of Og king of Bashan; the land, according to its cities and borders, even the cities of the surrounding land."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 32:39 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The children of Machir the son of Manasseh went to Gilead, took it, and dispossessed the Amorites who were therein."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 32:40 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Moses gave Gilead to Machir the son of Manasseh; and he lived therein."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 32:41 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Jair the son of Manasseh went and took its villages, and called them Havvoth Jair."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 34:14 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "for the tribe of the children of Reuben according to their fathers’ houses, the tribe of the children of Gad according to their fathers’ houses, and the half-tribe of Manasseh have received their inheritance."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 34:23 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Of the children of Joseph: of the tribe of the children of Manasseh a prince, Hanniel the son of Ephod."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 36:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "The heads of the fathers’ households of the family of the children of Gilead, the son of Machir, the son of Manasseh, of the families of the sons of Joseph, came near and spoke before Moses and before the princes, the heads of the fathers’ households of the children of Israel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "NUM 36:12 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "They were married into the families of the sons of Manasseh the son of Joseph. Their inheritance remained in the tribe of the family of their father."
      }
    ],
